Subject: [PATCH] media: sc4336p: accept the T31 CIM xclk

The T31 CGU derives the CIM MCLK from VPLL: 1200 MHz / 45 = 26.667 MHz,
not 27 MHz, so the exact-rate check fails probe with -EINVAL and no
sensor registers. The 1.2% error is inside the sensor's xclk tolerance;
accept a 2% window, as gc4023/gc8613 already accept a window.

Measured: /proc/jz/clock cgu_cim 26.666MHz on a T31X (Wuuk Y0510).
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/sc4336p.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/sc4336p.c
@@ -923,7 +923,8 @@
 				     "failed to get xclk\n");
 
 	xclk_freq = clk_get_rate(sc4336p->xclk);
-	if (xclk_freq != SC4336P_XCLK_FREQ)
+	if (xclk_freq < SC4336P_XCLK_FREQ - SC4336P_XCLK_FREQ / 50 ||
+	    xclk_freq > SC4336P_XCLK_FREQ + SC4336P_XCLK_FREQ / 50)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL,
 				     "xclk frequency %lu Hz not supported\n",
 				     xclk_freq);
